  "S5": {
   "id": "S5",
   "kind": "document",
   "title": "Statistics Estimators And Bias",
   "text": "3. The Bootstrap\nThe bootstrap estimates the uncertainty of a statistic by resampling. Draw n observations with\nreplacement from the original sample of size n, compute the statistic, and repeat this B times, for\nexample B = 1000. The spread of the B statistics approximates the sampling variability.\nA bootstrap percentile interval for 95% confidence uses the 2.5th and the 97.5th percentiles of the\nB bootstrap statistics. The bootstrap needs no formula for the standard error, which makes it useful\nfor medians and other awkward statistics.",
